Let the integrator decide, per inbound offer, whether the client engages the call at all.

Origin: fazer-ai/whatsapp-connector, upstream meowcaller code (not from a pull request).

Why: the connector builds the meowcaller client when it builds the whatsmeow client,
before it knows whether the session that is about to connect asked for calls to be
answered (`calls.answer`), and the client cannot be installed later, once whatsmeow is
connected. Without a gate, onOffer preaccepts every offer as soon as it arrives, which
announces this device as ringing for every call on an account whose client never asked
for calls: the account's phone and its other devices see a linked device join a call it
will never answer.

WithOfferGate is consulted at the top of onOffer, after the stale-offer mark is consumed
and before anything is sent or recorded. A refused offer gets no preaccept, no engine
entry and no OnIncomingCall, which covers group offers as well. Without the option every
offer is engaged, as before.

